	abstract = {Objectives: The use of tumor-informed circulating tumor {DNA} ({ctDNA}) testing in patients with early-stage disease before surgery is limited, mainly owing to restricted tissue access and extended turnaround times. This study aimed to evaluate the clinical value of a tumor-naïve, methylation-based cell-free {DNA} assay in a large cohort of patients with resected {NSCLC}.},
